  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge exchange sessions on Climate and Water Smart Agriculture (CaWSA) at Wadi Expo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to contribute to climate and water smart agriculture in Egypt, by connecting Dutch providers of agricultural technology, knowledge and services with clients, partners and beneficiaries in Upper Egypt.It will consist of knowledge and inspiration activities connected to the Wadi Expo in Luxor from 8-11 May, including1.	a field trip to SME farmers and smallholders farming on consolidated lands in Upper Egypt;2.	matchmaking and company presentation at the Wadi Expo in Luxor;3.	a seminar on climate and water smart agriculture;4.	a demonstration-day with Dutch companies and (potential) Egyptian partners.These activities will contribute to improved knowledge of Egyptian SMEs regarding Climate and Water-Smart Agriculture. and how the Netherlands can play a supporting role in that. Furthermore, the Dutch business community will be better informed of the local situation and needs. This project should inspire further business cases and interventions under the combi-trajectory.</narrative>
  </description>
